**Bug Fixed:** The issue was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` instead of `parts[0]`, which meant it was returning the second word instead of the first word. This caused the test_basic to fail (returning 'world' instead of 'hello') and test_single to crash with an IndexError (trying to access index 1 when only index 0 exists).

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]` to correctly return the first element of the split string.
